// 2026-11-01-dual3090-maya-glm.jsonc — Project Maya concurrency and long-context
// behaviour on the main GPU server (dual RTX 3090, PCIe 4.0 x16 cap / x8 actual).
//
// Question: does the pinned upstream Maya build serve concurrent requests at all
// on this pair, and at what cost, on the GLM-5.3-Flash S24 artifact?
//
// The earlier night run measured this engine as serializing requests. That
// measurement was taken on an older build and without the parallel flag, so it
// is not a property of the engine — it is a property of the configuration that
// was used. This campaign re-measures it with the concurrency gate (overlap
// proof) so a serialized engine cannot score as if it were parallel.
//
// No roster change is claimed; this produces a candidate for review.
{
  "id": "2026-11-01-dual3090-maya-glm",
  "question": "does the pinned upstream Maya build serve concurrent requests on this pair, and at what decode cost, on the GLM-5.3-Flash S24 artifact",
  "owner": "mf",
  "model": {
    "name": "glm-5.3-flash-maya-s24",
    "quant": "IQ2_XXS",
